The Jesus Family Series
This is the genealogy of the family of Jesus Christ. He was born of David. He was born of Abraham.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. Isaac was the father of Jacob. Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Judah was the father of Perez and Zerah. Their mother was Tamar. Perez was the father of Hezron. Hezron was the father of Ram.
Ram was the father of Amminadab. Amminadab was the father of Nahshon. Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Salem was Boaz's father. Rahab was Boaz's mother. Boaz was Obed's father. Ruth was Obed's mother. Obed was Jesse's father.
And Jesse was the father of King David. David was the father of Solomon. The mother of Solomon was the wife of Uriah.
Solomon was the father of Rehoboam. Rehoboam was the father of Abijah. Abijah was the father of Asa.
A stick was the father of Jehoshaphat. Jehoshaphat was the father of Joram. Joram was the father of Uzziah.
Azariah was the father of Jotham. Jotham was the father of Ahaz. Ahaz was the father of Hezekiah.
Hezekiah was the father of Manasseh. Manasseh was the father of Amon. Amon was the father of Josiah.
Josiah was the father of Jeconiah and his brothers. At that time, the Jewish people were forced to go to Babylon.
From that time on, the family line continued. Jeconiah was the father of Salathiel. Salathiel was the father of Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel was the father of Abiud. Abiud was the father of Eliakim. Eliakim was the father of Azor.
Azor was the father of Zadok. Zadok was the father of Akim. Akim was the father of Eliud.
Eliohu was the father of Eliezer. Eliezer was the father of Matan. Matan was the father of Yaakov.
Jacob was the father of Joseph. Joseph was the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Christ.
There were 14 generations from Abraham to David. And there were 14 from David until the Jews were forced to walk to Babylon. And there were 14 from that time until Christ. Jesus Christ was born.
Thus, the birth of Jesus Christ came about. His mother was Mary, and Joseph, who were betrothed to be married. But before they came together, it was found that she was with child. She was conceived by the power of the Holy Spirit.
Her husband, Youssef, was a pious man. He did not want to expose her to the public. Therefore, he decided to divorce her in a quiet manner.
But while Joseph was thinking about this, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream. The angel said to him, "Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary into your home as your wife. The child within her was conceived by the Holy Spirit."
She will give birth to a son. You shall give him the name Jesus. For he will save his people from their sins.
All this happened to fulfill what the Lord had said through the prophet,
The virgin will conceive and give birth to a son. She will call him Immanuel. (Isaiah 7:14) The name Immanuel means "God with us."
Joseph did as the angel of the Lord commanded him; he took Mary into his home as his wife.
But he didn't talk to her at all, even after she gave birth to a son. And Joseph named him Jesus.
The wise men visit Jesus.
Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea. This happened while Herod was king of Judea. After Jesus was born, wise men from the east came to Jerusalem.
They said, "Where is the child who has been born to be king of the Jews? For we have seen his star in the east and have come to worship him."
When King Herod heard about this, he was deeply disturbed. And it distressed everyone in Jerusalem.
Herod called together all the chief priests of the people, and the teachers of the law. He asked them where the Messiah would be born.
"In Bethlehem of Judea," they answered him. "For this is what the prophet has written. 'And you, Bethlehem, in the land of Judah, are by no means least among the rulers of Judah; for out of you will come a ruler who will shepherd my people Israel.'"
"But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, though you are small among the clans of Judah, out of you will come one who will be ruler over Israel, whose origins are from of old, from ancient times." (Micah 5:2)
Afterwards, Herod secretly called the wise men. He learned from them exactly when the star appeared.
Send them to Bethlehem. He told them, "Go! Search diligently for the child. When you find him, bring me word. So that I may come and worship him also."
After the wise men had heard the king, they went on their way. The star that they had seen when they were in the east went before them. And in the end it stopped above the place where the child was.
When they saw the star, they were filled with joy.
The wise men went to the house. There they saw the child with his mother Mary. They knelt down and worshipped him. Then they opened their treasures. They gave him gold, frankincense and myrrh.
But God warned them, so he dreamt that they should not return to Herod. So they returned to their own country by another way. The family of Jesus fled to Egypt.
When the wise men had gone, Joseph had a dream. In his dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him. The angel said to him, "Get up! Take the child and his mother and flee to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you to return. Herod is going to look for the child. He wants to kill him."
Joseph got up. At night, he went to Egypt with the child and his mother Mary.
They remained there until King Herod died. And those words which the Lord spoke by the prophet were fulfilled, saying, "Out of Egypt I have called my son." (Hosea 11:1)
Herod realized that the wise men had deceived him. He became very angry. He gave orders concerning Bethlehem and the surrounding area. It was decreed that all the male children in Bethlehem and its vicinity who were two years old or less were to be killed. This was in agreement with the timing indicated by the star that the wise men had seen.
In this way, the words spoken by the prophet Jeremiah were fulfilled. He said,
